CSPro logic <link user_defined_functions.csdoc>user-defined functions</link> can be used as arguments. With the following JavaScript script <link manage_application_files.csdoc>added to the application</link>...

<color JavaScript>
function getCSProVersion(diagnosticsCallback) {
    return diagnosticsCallback("version");
}
</color>

...it is possible to call into JavaScript and then have JavaScript call back into CSPro.

<logic>
function string ExecDiagnostics(string property)
    exit diagnostics(property);
end;

JS.invoke("getCSProVersion", ExecDiagnostics)); // <definition CSPro::version />
diagnostics("version");                         // <definition CSPro::version />
</logic>